{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Bag of Words, TF-IDF, and Text Representation Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: build the vocabulary"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def build_vocab(docs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    vocab = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for doc in docs:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for token in doc:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if token not in vocab:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                vocab[token] = len(vocab)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return vocab"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Input: list of tokenized documents (any word-level tokenizer will do; the `code/main.py` in this lesson uses a simplified lowercase variant). Output: `{word: index}` dict. Stable insertion order means word index 0 is the first word seen in the first document. Convention varies; scikit-learn sorts alphabetically."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: bag of words"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def bag_of_words(docs, vocab):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    matrix = [[0] * len(vocab) for _ in docs]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, doc in enumerate(docs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for token in doc:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if token in vocab:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                matrix[i][vocab[token]] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return matrix"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> docs = [[\"cat\", \"sat\", \"on\", \"mat\"], [\"cat\", \"cat\", \"ran\"]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> vocab = build_vocab(docs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> bag_of_words(docs, vocab)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "[[1, 1, 1, 1, 0], [2, 0, 0, 0, 1]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Rows are documents. Columns are vocabulary indices. Entry `[i][j]` is \"how many times word `j` appears in document `i`.\" Doc 1 has `cat` twice because it did. Doc 0 has `ran` zero times because it did not."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: term frequency and document frequency"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def term_frequency(doc_bow, doc_length):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [c / doc_length if doc_length else 0 for c in doc_bow]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def document_frequency(bow_matrix):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    df = [0] * len(bow_matrix[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for row in bow_matrix:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for j, count in enumerate(row):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if count > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                df[j] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return df"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def inverse_document_frequency(df, n_docs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [math.log((n_docs + 1) / (d + 1)) + 1 for d in df]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Two smoothing tricks worth naming. The `(n+1)/(d+1)` avoids `log(x/0)`. The trailing `+1` ensures a word in every document still has IDF 1 (not 0), matching scikit-learn's default. Other implementations use raw `log(N/df)`. Both work; the smoothed version is friendlier."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: TF-IDF"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def tfidf(bow_matrix):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_docs = len(bow_matrix)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    df = document_frequency(bow_matrix)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    idf = inverse_document_frequency(df, n_docs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for row in bow_matrix:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        length = sum(row)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tf = term_frequency(row, length)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out.append([tf_j * idf_j for tf_j, idf_j in zip(tf, idf)])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> docs = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "...     [\"the\", \"cat\", \"sat\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "...     [\"the\", \"dog\", \"sat\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "...     [\"the\", \"cat\", \"ran\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "... ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> vocab = build_vocab(docs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> bow = bag_of_words(docs, vocab)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> tfidf(bow)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three documents, five vocab words (`the`, `cat`, `sat`, `dog`, `ran`). `the` appears in all three, so its IDF is low. `dog` appears in one, so its IDF is high. The vectors are sparse (most entries are small) and the discriminative words pop."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: L2-normalize rows"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def l2_normalize(matrix):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for row in matrix:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        norm = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in row))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out.append([x / norm if norm else 0 for x in row])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Without normalization, a longer document gets a larger vector and dominates similarity scores. L2 normalization puts every document on the unit hypersphere. Cosine similarity between rows is now just a dot product."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Implement `cosine_similarity(doc_vec_a, doc_vec_b)` on the L2-normalized TF-IDF output. Verify that identical documents score 1.0 and disjoint-vocabulary documents score 0.0.\n2. **Medium.** Add `n-gram` support to `bag_of_words`. Parameter `n` produces counts over `n`-grams. Test that `n=2` on `[\"the\", \"cat\", \"sat\"]` produces bigram counts for `[\"the cat\", \"cat sat\"]`.\n3. **Hard.** Build the TF-IDF-weighted-embedding hybrid above using GloVe 100d vectors (download once, cache). Compare classification accuracy against plain TF-IDF and plain mean-pooled embeddings on the 20 Newsgroups dataset. Report which wins where."
      ]
    }
